id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20240220","date":"2024-02-20","original_code":"746.4901(a)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-03-20","finding":"Active Play Surfacing In Use Zones - Loose Fill or Unitary Surfacing: In the outdoor area there are four slides, three slides were without loose-fill. One slide had loose-fill that is not the required 6 inches of depth due to mesh being exposed which can cause a trip hazard for children. Three of the four slides were removed from the outdoor play area.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026444025","violation_type_title":"Active Play Surfacing In Use Zones - Loose Fill or Unitary Surfacing (26 TAC §746.4901(a))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20240220-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3407-5","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20240220","date":"2024-02-20","original_code":"746.3407(5)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Sanitize Potty-Chairs: In multiple classroom/bathrooms, the potty chairs were not emptied after use due to urine sitting in the bottom of the potty chairs. This was corrected at inspection once the potty chairs were emptied.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026404240","violation_type_title":"Sanitize Potty-Chairs (26 TAC §746.3407(5))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231211","date":"2023-12-11","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905827325","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905827325","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2023-12-11","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129","date":"2023-11-29","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":6,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905827324","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905827324","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2023-11-29","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2909-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129","date":"2023-11-29","original_code":"746.2909(4)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-12-11","finding":"Arrangement of Napping Equipment - Provides Access to Walkway: The napping arrangement in one classroom made it difficult to walk in the room without having to step over children.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026248610","violation_type_title":"Arrangement of Napping Equipment - Provides Access to Walkway (26 TAC §746.2909(4))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-4751-a","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129","date":"2023-11-29","original_code":"746.4751(a)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-12-11","finding":"Maintenance Procedures for Active Play - Inspect Daily: There were multiple hazards observed that presented risk to children:  *The under lining around the playground border was exposed posing a tripping hazard.  * There were sharp metal wires accessible on the fence posing an injury hazard if children were too close to the fence.  *There were wood logs deteriorating on the playground that could cause insect infestation to the playground area.  *There was a gap in the wire fence wide enough to fit the child's head and extremities.  *There was a gap at the bottom of the wood fence wide enough to fit the feet of children, to become a tripping or entanglement hazard and expose the grounds to environmental hazards.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026529617","violation_type_title":"Maintenance Procedures for Active Play - Inspect Daily (26 TAC §746.4751(a))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-4805-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129","date":"2023-11-29","original_code":"746.4805(b)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-12-11","finding":"Measurement of Use Zone for Slides - Six Feet High or Less: There was one slide that did not meet the 6 feet use zone requirements. The slide was too close and overlapped with the border that surrounds the slide.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026329114","violation_type_title":"Measurement of Use Zone for Slides - Six Feet High or Less (26 TAC §746.4805(b))","topic_label":"Other"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-745-651-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129","date":"2023-11-29","original_code":"745.651(1)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-12-06","finding":"Background Check Validation - You must inactivate a subject who is no longer associated with your operation within 7 days of leaving: There was one background check that has been pending since 10/16/2023.     There was a total of 8 subjects on the background check list that were no longer associated with the operation. The background check people list was last validated on 10/29/2023.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026369369","violation_type_title":"Background Check Validation - You must inactivate a subject who is no longer associated with your operation within 7 days of leaving (26 TAC §745.651(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-605-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129","date":"2023-11-29","original_code":"746.605(3)","severity":"medium_low","severity_label":"Medium-low risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-12-11","finding":"Required Admission Information - Date of Admission: Of the 6 children records reviewed, 3 files were missing the date of admissions for the children.  * 4 children files were missing the address and phone number for the person listed as the emergency contact per 746.605(6).   * 3 of the 6 children files were missing the Authorized Emergency care facilities address and phone number per 746.605(11)  * 2 of the 6 children files were missing the Special Needs statements acknowledgement by the parents per 746.605 (13)(A).  * 1 of the 6 children files was missing the Authorized Release person's name and phone number per 746.605(7).","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026489159","violation_type_title":"Required Admission Information - Date of Admission (26 TAC §746.605(3))","topic_label":"Fire safety & emergency drills"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1315685-i20231129","date":"2023-11-29","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-12-11","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: There was one child observed napping in the kitchen area outside of the classroom, due to discipline. * This was corrected at inspection when the child was moved back into the classroom population.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026369367","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §